    "['set protocols ospf area [area_id]', [{'para_map': [], 'trans_command': 'ospf 1', 'parent_command': [], 'root': 'ospf 1', 'source': 'llm', 'origin_reponse': 'Here\\'s the equivalent HUAWEI router configuration for the given Juniper OSPF interface commands:\\n\\n##\\nospf 1\\n area 0.0.0.0\\n  network 172.16.1.1 0.0.0.0\\n  p2mp enable\\n##\\n\\nNote:\\n1. In HUAWEI, OSPF configuration starts with \"ospf <process-id>\" (I used 1 as default)\\n2. The \"network\" command specifies the interface IP with wildcard mask (0.0.0.0 means exact match)\\n3. The \"p2mp enable\" command sets the interface type to point-to-multipoint\\n4. The area configuration is nested under the OSPF process', 'trans_template': 'ospf 1'}, {'para_map': [], 'trans_command': 'area 0.0.0.0', 'parent_command': [], 'root': 'area 0.0.0.0', 'source': 'llm', 'origin_reponse': 'Here\\'s the equivalent HUAWEI router configuration for the given Juniper OSPF interface commands:\\n\\n##\\nospf 1\\n area 0.0.0.0\\n  network 172.16.1.1 0.0.0.0\\n  p2mp enable\\n##\\n\\nNote:\\n1. In HUAWEI, OSPF configuration starts with \"ospf <process-id>\" (I used 1 as default)\\n2. The \"network\" command specifies the interface IP with wildcard mask (0.0.0.0 means exact match)\\n3. The \"p2mp enable\" command sets the interface type to point-to-multipoint\\n4. The area configuration is nested under the OSPF process', 'trans_template': 'area 0.0.0.0'}, {'para_map': [], 'trans_command': 'network 172.16.1.1 0.0.0.0', 'parent_command': [], 'root': 'network 172.16.1.1 0.0.0.0', 'source': 'llm', 'origin_reponse': 'Here\\'s the equivalent HUAWEI router configuration for the given Juniper OSPF interface commands:\\n\\n##\\nospf 1\\n area 0.0.0.0\\n  network 172.16.1.1 0.0.0.0\\n  p2mp enable\\n##\\n\\nNote:\\n1. In HUAWEI, OSPF configuration starts with \"ospf <process-id>\" (I used 1 as default)\\n2. The \"network\" command specifies the interface IP with wildcard mask (0.0.0.0 means exact match)\\n3. The \"p2mp enable\" co